			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-11T17:48:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1505,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(GITEX): wrap git subprocess with a 30s timeout (#55)\n\ntokio::process::Command::new(\"git\").output().await had no\ncancellation boundary. A slow or hanging git operation (large\nrepo, network mount, credential prompt, locked index) would\nhold the effect slot open indefinitely.\n\nWrap with tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(30), ...).\nOn expiry the child process is abandoned and a descriptive Err\nis returned so the extension host can surface the failure.\n\nThe 30s ceiling is generous enough for legitimate slow clones\nover gRPC but tight enough to prevent indefinite hangs. The\nelapsed dev_log is kept so timing is still observable in logs.",
			"SHA": "4215c8a141c82a6bd07e3e642eccc2e4b3cade9e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-11T17:48:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1505,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(WSAE): propagate Err from applyEdit instead of synthetic true (#54)\n\nWhen Sky does not answer sky://workspace/applyEdit, returning\nOk(json!(true)) causes every extension that checks the boolean\nresult of `workspace.applyEdit()` to believe the edit succeeded\nand proceed against post-apply state that never materialised.\n\nPropagate the error instead so the extension host surfaces the\nfailure correctly. showTextDocument already uses Ok(json!(null))\non its failure path; this aligns applyEdit with that safer\npattern while going one step further and returning a real Err\nso callers can distinguish a Sky failure from a successful\nfalse-result from the provider.",
			"SHA": "fc59918c8e1ce7045b50bccabc57e23344167604"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-11T17:43:39Z",
			"File": [
